theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038412/assets/0d901312b6a14c863085276458cf8341cbd4cb6cc5411d5c5045244b8c656eb2.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that inside our region, the spherical polar coordinates vary withing the following domains:\n\n- $\\rho \\in [0,2]$\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fde60ded-ec05-5a2c-8844-26e8e02c9afb" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Part of a Sphere in Spherical Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132e2a6d-3671-56ed-91f8-fea5f8ac2e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 36,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312393} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7449a4-1984-51a8-aeb6-19b84165dda2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 12,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312394} {:answer/id #uuid "58004e6f-2afc-5b50-a08d-3df8a1c388c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 6,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312395} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8bfeb4-0529-5275-8ed6-4051574e2c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 6,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312396} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a95d91-b343-5964-ab91-7d915fd3c31